---
import Study from "../../layouts/Study.astro";
---

<Study
  title="OmniStream Database Project"
  kind="Projects"
  status="Database design / Coursework"
  repo="OmniStream-Database-System"
  deck="A PostgreSQL coursework project that works through the structure and behaviour of a video-streaming database."
>
  <div class="study-grid">
    <aside>
      <p>Focus</p>
      <span>
        Relational design
        <br />
        Analytical SQL
        <br />
        Transactions
      </span>
    </aside>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Make the relationships explicit.</h2>
      <p>
        The schema covers users, plans, subscriptions, payments, invoices,
        movies, genres, watchlists, viewing history and reviews. Keys and
        constraints establish relationships; seed data supplies an inspection
        environment.
      </p>
      <p>
        The SQL explores joins, aggregation and JSONB metadata, including a GIN
        index. The design report discusses normalization. No measured
        performance study is included, so the index is presented as an
        implementation choice rather than a proven speedup.
      </p>
      <h2>A failure with a purpose.</h2>
      <p>
        A deliberately invalid invoice insert demonstrates a foreign-key failure
        and transaction rollback. That example is not a production migration.
        The ordered DDL and seed scripts provide the clearer route to recreating
        an example database.
      </p>
      <details>
        <summary>Repository structure</summary>
        <div>
          <p>
            <code>sql/DDL.sql</code> defines tables and constraints;{" "}
            <code>sql/DML.sql</code> supplies example data;{" "}
            <code>sql/DQL_and_TCL.sql</code> contains analytics, index creation
            and the rollback demonstration. Reports and editable diagrams are
            under <code>docs/</code>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </details>
      <div class="limitation">
        <h3>Scope</h3>
        <p>
          This is coursework, not a deployed streaming platform. The checked-in
          backup's restoration has not been independently verified here. No
          production scale, latency or commercial use is claimed.
        </p>
      </div>
      <a class="next-study" href="/projects/agent-router/">
        <small>Next project</small>
        <span>Huawei LLM Agent Router&nbsp;↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Study>
